{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## The code half is merged\n\nCommit `213341e3e58faf021f51ddd7db0285f57d95f2b9` (\"Grant Titan embedding ARN to Bedrock policy\") is an ancestor of `origin/main` (`git merge-base --is-ancestor` exits 0). Verified against the merged tree, not the branch:\n\n```\n$ git show origin/main:infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf | grep -n 'titan\\|sid'\n12:    sid = \"InvokeScopedBedrockModels\"\n20:      \"arn:aws:bedrock:*::foundation-model/amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0\",\n```\n\nBoth the Titan ARN and the renamed sid are live in `main`. All 14 codebase acceptance criteria are therefore satisfied in the merged tree, and the earlier comment's \"`make verify` has not yet run on this branch\" is superseded: the change passed CI's `Verified` gate as a condition of merging.\n\n## What is left\n\nOnly the `[non-codebase]` criterion: an operator applies the Terraform and records an attestation here carrying the Gerrit change number, the revision SHA, the UTC timestamp, the dimension count from a real Titan embedding call made from the Gerrit instance role, and the operator identity.\n\nThat is an AWS apply plus a live credential-bearing call. It cannot be performed or attested from an agent session, and the ticket's own Approach section explains why no substitute exists: `.github/workflows/terraform-drift.yml` is not fired by a Gerrit change, applies run manually through `scripts/terraform_prod.py`, and a policy simulator cannot settle it because Converse authorizes against `bedrock:InvokeModel` while the distinct `bedrock:Converse` action simulates as denied.\n\nThe ticket stays `in_progress` pending that attestation. Note that it is not a feature blocker: the lexical tier needs no model provider, and the embedding tier is unset by default and degrades to lexical when the provider is absent or denies.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793617769905267607,"uuid":"0a1b907f-37e3-4a70-b647-55bf2a0ec5bd"}